        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0258" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1548</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1118</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 14, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my despatches Nos. 1080 and
                    1082 of May 17 last, and referring to my telegram of June 13, 8 p.m. I have the
                    honor to enclose herewith the translation of a note, dated the 10th instant,
                    with which the Foreign Office transmitted to the Legation a copy of the English
                    text of an agreement and two supplementary agreements, with respect to the
                    construction of certain railways, between the Ministry of Communications and Mr.
                    W. F. Carey, representing the Siems-Carey Company.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul S. Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>






